# The Monuments window (MonuWin, see monuwin.c), opened with the script host's steps: mon_14a gives faction 1 fourteen monuments
# (kinds 0 to 13, dated out of order, the even kinds the faction's own first), and monument_list opens the window on its list
# (monument(0)). The window is the big one, at the corner of the screen; the icons stand in fourteen places in the order of their
# dates (slot 0 kind 0, slot 1 kind 13, slot 7 kind 1, ...). The list as it opens; the mouse over an icon (it draws that
# monument's picture, kind 13 being the faction's own), over the picture shown (nothing) and off every icon; a click zooms an icon
# (moves are then ignored), a click anywhere goes back; a click on the picture shown zooms the one last shown; Return goes
# back; the button (at the foot, to the right) goes back and, from the list, closes. The state regions are the faction's
# monument records (with the kind shown), the window object's working numbers (the corner, the rectangles, the zoom flag, the
# kind last shown), the places of its pictures, the count of monuments, and the text variables the words are built from.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
25 load
42 state mon 0x94ca08 0x2780
42 state work 0x7fa96c 0x44
42 state rects 0x7fd08c 0x110
42 state pairs 0x7fd2a4 0x60
42 state faces 0x7fd5c4 0x70
42 state count 0x7fd634 4
42 state parse 0x9bb570 0xa84
44 open mon_14a
46 open monument_list
52 snap list
54 move 435 530
57 snap hover-first
59 move 589 530
62 snap hover-own
64 move 704 478
67 snap hover-icon
69 move 512 220
72 snap hover-view
74 move 20 20
77 snap hover-off
79 click 704 478
83 snap zoomed
85 move 435 530
88 snap zoomed-move
90 click 300 300
94 snap list-again
96 click 512 220
100 snap zoom-view
102 key Return
106 snap key-back
108 click 704 478
112 snap zoomed-2
114 click 924 757
118 snap button-back
120 click 924 757
126 snap closed
130 close
